  "prompt": "A surreal, editorially precise image captures a lone runner on a narrow path winding through a perfectly still, mirror-like salt flat, where sky and earth dissolve into one another in seamless cobalt reflection. The path stretches forward like an infinite runway, floating in the horizonless expanse a line of quiet defiance cutting through eternity. The runner, mid-stride, is framed with minimalist precision: a small yet commanding figure suspended between two worlds, their reflection so crisp it feels like another being running beneath the surface of the maroon body of water. The air is motionless, the light a painterly fusion of early-morning gold and deep cerulean, creating a tone both sacred and surreal. Ripples of reflected sky shimmer faintly around the runner’s path, amplifying the illusion that they are sprinting across light itself. Captured on a Phase One XF IQ4 150MP with an 80mm Schneider Kreuznach LS f/2.8 Blue Ring, at f/5.6, ISO 50, 1/800s, the image balances hyperreal sharpness with cinematic tranquility. Graded through the Loewe SS25 Horizon Mirror LUT, processed in 16-bit Open Gate RAW, and archived under the Vogue Italia Infinity Motion Series, file IMG_8239.IIQ, this photograph reads like a visual haiku a study in solitude, precision, and the poetry of motion suspended within an endless reflection, where the act of running becomes the quiet architecture of infinity. --ar 9:16 --raw --profile 8kbzn1r --stylize 50",
